From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 15:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SnpDxe: accept a USB ancestor where a PCI one is absent

SimpleNetworkDriverStart refused any UNDI without an EFI_PCI_IO_PROTOCOL in
its device path ancestry:

    Status = gBS->LocateDevicePath (&gEfiPciIoProtocolGuid, &NiiDevicePath, &Handle);
    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
      return Status;
    }

That rejects a whole class of adapter before any work is done. On a Raspberry
Pi 5 the same USB CDC-NCM gadget binds on the RP1 xHCI ports, whose device
path is rooted in PCI because RP1 is a PCIe device, and is refused on the
BCM2712 DWC2 port, whose host controller publishes a bare vendor-hardware
device path. The symptom is quiet: Supported() succeeds and logs,
NetworkCommon publishes its NII, and Start() returns before its first DEBUG
line, so an EFI_SIMPLE_NETWORK_PROTOCOL never appears and every consumer above
it -- MNP, ARP, IPv4, TCP, and in this case a Redfish host interface over
RestEx -- reports only that its own dependency is missing.

Keep PciIo as the default and preferred case, and accept a USB ancestor as the
alternative. EFI_USB_IO_PROTOCOL exposes no DMA surface at all -- no
AllocateBuffer, no Map, no Unmap -- and needs none: the USB host controller
driver owns the bus mastering, bounce buffering included, so a USB UNDI
performs its own I/O and never asks SNP to translate an address. Finding UsbIo
in the ancestry is proof that the PciIo services are not required, not a
substitute for them. A UNDI on neither bus is still refused.

PciIo is used for three things, and each has an answer without it:

  - The CPB/DB/CDB and Tx/Rx allocations. Route them through new
    SnpAllocateBuffer/SnpFreeBuffer helpers that use AllocateBuffer/FreeBuffer
    when PciIo is present and page allocation when it is not. A UNDI that
    performs its own I/O -- any software UNDI, such as the USB network class
    drivers in MdeModulePkg -- only ever has the CPU touch these structures.

  - The BAR scan that fills MemoryBarIndex and IoBarIndex. Skip it, leaving
    both at PCI_MAX_BAR. The Io and Mem UNDI callbacks already test for that
    before use, so they become inert; their ASSERTs are widened to accept the
    no-PciIo case, which would otherwise deadloop a DEBUG build the first time
    a UNDI issued one of those callbacks.

  - The Map and Unmap UNDI callbacks. Refuse cleanly instead of dereferencing
    NULL. A UNDI that asks SNP to translate an address is asking for a DMA
    mapping this driver cannot provide, and saying so beats faulting.

SimpleNetworkDriverFree already tested Snp->PciIo for NULL before releasing
the CPB/DB/CDB, so a NULL PciIo was half-anticipated here; it now uses the
same helper as the allocation path so the fallback is released correctly.

The failed-PciIo path also now closes the device path protocol it opened
BY_DRIVER before returning, which the original bare return leaked.

Declare MemoryAllocationLib and gEfiUsbIoProtocolGuid in the INF.
AllocateZeroPool and FreePool were already used and resolved transitively;
AllocatePages and FreePages make the dependency worth stating.

Behaviour is unchanged for every adapter that has a PCI ancestor: PciIo is
found on the first lookup, and the same allocator and the same BAR scan run as
before. The only paths that change are the one that previously failed outright
and the leak on its way out.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
---
--- a/NetworkPkg/SnpDxe/Snp.h
+++ b/NetworkPkg/SnpDxe/Snp.h
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include <Library/PrintLib.h>
 #include <Library/PcdLib.h>
 
+#include <Protocol/UsbIo.h>
 #include <IndustryStandard/Pci.h>
 #include <IndustryStandard/Acpi.h>
 
@@ -1027,3 +1028,38 @@
   );
 
 #define SNP_MEM_PAGES(x)  (((x) - 1) / 4096 + 1)
+
+/**
+  Allocate a buffer for the UNDI CPB/DB/CDB or Tx/Rx structures.
+
+  Uses EFI_PCI_IO_PROTOCOL.AllocateBuffer when the UNDI has a PCI ancestor
+  and plain page allocation when it does not. See SimpleNetworkDriverStart
+  for why PciIo is optional.
+
+  @param  Snp     Driver instance.
+  @param  Pages   Number of pages to allocate.
+  @param  Buffer  Receives the allocation.
+
+  @retval EFI_SUCCESS           Allocated.
+  @retval EFI_OUT_OF_RESOURCES  Not allocated.
+**/
+EFI_STATUS
+SnpAllocateBuffer (
+  IN  SNP_DRIVER  *Snp,
+  IN  UINTN       Pages,
+  OUT VOID        **Buffer
+  );
+
+/**
+  Release a buffer obtained from SnpAllocateBuffer.
+
+  @param  Snp     Driver instance.
+  @param  Pages   Number of pages originally requested.
+  @param  Buffer  The allocation to release.
+**/
+VOID
+SnpFreeBuffer (
+  IN SNP_DRIVER  *Snp,
+  IN UINTN       Pages,
+  IN VOID        *Buffer
+  );
--- a/NetworkPkg/SnpDxe/Snp.c
+++ b/NetworkPkg/SnpDxe/Snp.c
@@ -240,39 +240,63 @@
 
   @param  Snp   Pointer to SNP_DRIVER structure to be freed.
 **/
+EFI_STATUS
+SnpAllocateBuffer (
+  IN  SNP_DRIVER  *Snp,
+  IN  UINTN       Pages,
+  OUT VOID        **Buffer
+  )
+{
+  if (Snp->PciIo != NULL) {
+    return Snp->PciIo->AllocateBuffer (
+                         Snp->PciIo,
+                         AllocateAnyPages,
+                         EfiBootServicesData,
+                         Pages,
+                         Buffer,
+                         0
+                         );
+  }
+
+  *Buffer = AllocatePages (Pages);
+  if (*Buffer == NULL) {
+    return EFI_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+  }
+
+  return EFI_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+VOID
+SnpFreeBuffer (
+  IN SNP_DRIVER  *Snp,
+  IN UINTN       Pages,
+  IN VOID        *Buffer
+  )
+{
+  if (Snp->PciIo != NULL) {
+    Snp->PciIo->FreeBuffer (Snp->PciIo, Pages, Buffer);
+    return;
+  }
+
+  FreePages (Buffer, Pages);
+}
+
 VOID
 SimpleNetworkDriverFree (
   IN SNP_DRIVER  *Snp
   )
 {
-  EFI_PCI_IO_PROTOCOL  *PciIo;
-
   if (Snp != NULL) {
